INT. NORTHWIND LOGISTICS - ESCAPE ROOM "THE VAULT OF SYNERGY" - DAY

A windowless basement fitted as a movie-set bank. Brass safe doors, laser-beam strips of red tape, a ticking digital clock above the mantel: 59:12.

Six employees in matching fleece vests stand in a ring around a locked chest. Lanyards. Name tags. Forced smiles.

DIRECTOR GREGOR HALVORSEN, 50s, bald, a vest zipped to the chin, claps once.

GREGOR
Team! Remember. There's no "I" in--

PRIYA NAIR, 30s, accountant, glances at her watch.

PRIYA
We've got fifty-eight minutes.

GREGOR
Alignment is a journey.

TODD BEXLEY, 40s, sales, taps the chest.

TODD
It's a padlock. Four digits.

GREGOR
Who has the clue?

BEATRICE KOWALSKI, 60s, HR, lifts a laminated card with a trembling hand.

BEATRICE
"The date of our greatest quarter."

TODD
That's every quarter.

GREGOR
Todd.

TODD
I'm saying, it's every quarter.

MARCUS ELLIOT, 20s, junior analyst, stares at the clock.

MARCUS
Fifty-six minutes.

GREGOR
Marcus, please. We don't count down. We count up.

Marcus nods. Counts nothing. His left eye twitches.

DELILAH OKONJO, 40s, procurement, stands with her arms crossed, in the corner.

DELILAH
It's seventeen forty-two.

GREGOR
Is that a guess?

DELILAH
It's on the whiteboard behind you.

They all turn. A whiteboard reads: FOUNDED 1742. Gregor's smile fixes in place.

GREGOR
Great catch, Delilah.

Priya enters the code. The padlock clicks. The chest opens. Inside, a single laminated card: CONGRATULATIONS. PLEASE COMPLETE THE SURVEY.

Nobody speaks. Todd picks up the card, turns it over.

TODD
There's a QR code.

BEATRICE
Of course there is.

They stand there, six fleece vests in a basement, while the clock beeps. 54:03. 54:02.
